1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,700
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:18,460
After sitting inside the magnetic field for 800 years, Avon's greatest tool, brew, has ceased to function.

3
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:23,820
And so, here we are. There is no more time to fool around.

4
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:30,160
Fortunately, the DWMA knows only that we have brew, not that it's no longer operational.

5
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:35,980
Before they can recover from their latest failure, we should move on to the next step of our plan.

6
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,280
Wouldn't you agree, Mosquito?

7
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,640
Yes, Lady Arachne, I agree completely.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,300
How is our research on the moral manipulation machine progressing? Are we on schedule?

9
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:51,880
It's nearly complete. We're entering the final stages of research as we speak.

10
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,180
Faster than expected.

11
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,360
If we continue at this rate, it should be ready very soon.

12
00:00:58,580 --> 00:00:58,940
Yes.

13
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:02,000
Ha! What do we need with some stupid machine?

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,740
Why not just leave the Academy agents to me? I'll destroy them all.

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,920
Naturally, since you did such a good job of destroying them during the battle on Lost Island.

16
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:17,620
I pulled back my forces, assuming you could handle your part of the mission. Was I wrong?

17
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:22,280
You shouldn't presume to comment on my job performance. It could be hazardous to your health.

18
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:24,740
What are you saying, old geezer?

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:29,480
Shall I spell it out for you? Watch your mouth, or I'll beat you to a bloody pulp.

20
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:34,380
I'd like to see that. Come on, try me.

21
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,080
Enough squabbling, you two.

22
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:48,460
Now, Mosquito, continue with your report.

23
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:53,160
Yes. We've begun installing stations at various points around the world.

24
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:57,900
Construction continues swiftly and efficiently. Everything is proceeding as planned.

25
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:01,560
Good. Now for the next step.

26
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:12,660
My darling children, go forth. Complete the task your mother has given you.

27
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:20,000
At last, arachnophobia finally begins its rightful ascendancy.

28
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:41,140
I'm falling down to my shadow.

29
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:59,200
To begin with.

30
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:05,480
Don't ski.

31
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:12,480
It's a scary dream, but it's a terrible dream

32
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:15,480
For you, it's a terrible dream

33
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:18,480
For you, it's a terrible dream

34
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:23,480
I'm wearing a black paper

35
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:27,480
If you gave it to me

36
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:31,480
When you're lost, you're young

37
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:35,480
Forever with your soul

38
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,480
You're young, you're young

39
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:42,480
You're young

40
00:03:54,480 --> 00:04:00,480
And out of nowhere, we were besieged by hundreds of arachnophobia's most elite forces!

41
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,480
In the classroom, I may seem quiet

42
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:05,480
But in battle, all of that changes

43
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:11,480
In the end, all we managed to do was beat up on some old man and send him running back to arachnophobia

44
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:15,480
We don't even have brew to show for it

45
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,480
Nothing can change our failure

46
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,480
What happened?

47
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:32,480
Impossible! That technique's too advanced!

48
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,480
What he said when I used it

49
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,480
And that strange blast of light

50
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:42,480
Where did a move like that come from and how did I use it?

51
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,480
Is it connected to Sol's plane?

52
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:58,480
All we did was survive a small skirmish against one of the enemy

53
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,480
We gained absolutely nothing

54
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:06,480
Maybe I should talk to Lord Death about it

55
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:14,480
Everybody looks pretty depressed, huh?

56
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,480
It's not surprising

57
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:18,480
We risked a lot going to that island for a big fight

58
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:21,480
And arachnophobia still ended up with brew anyway

59
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,480
I know, but what's so depressing about that?

60
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:26,480
Why don't you sit quietly and think about it for a minute

61
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,480
Okay, sis, I'll try

62
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:34,480
By the way, what's up with Kid? I haven't seen him in a while

63
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:38,480
He said he was going to the bathroom, but now that you mention it, he has been gone a long time

64
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:42,480
What do you think he's gotten himself into now?

65
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:48,480
The detective's first case

66
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:51,480
Kid exposes the DWMA's secret?

67
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:00,480
What does the Academy know?

68
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:02,480
What does my father have planned?

69
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,480
What's he hiding?

70
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:07,480
He's been gathering every magic tool Abon created

71
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:11,480
He sent out the Academy troops to prevent brew from falling into the wrong hands

72
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,480
But he's not telling us everything

73
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:16,480
What are his true intentions?

74
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,480
What information has he been holding back?

75
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,480
I know there's more to this than there seems

76
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:26,480
Who is this great wizard Abon?

77
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:29,480
What does he have to do with my father?

78
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:35,480
I asked him about it and as expected he gave a half answer and then changed the subject

79
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:44,480
If he won't tell me, I'll find out for myself

80
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:45,480
Anyway, like I was saying, something's been bothering Kid lately. He seems a bit suspicious of your recent actions.

81
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,480
Hmm.

82
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,480
Hmm.

83
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,480
He's been poking around for information on his own. What should we do?

84
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,480
Hmm.

85
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,480
Hmm.

86
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,480
Poking around for information on his own. What should we do?

87
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,480
Poking around for information on his own. What should we do?

88
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:55,480
Poking around for information?

89
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,480
For information.

90
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,480
For information.

91
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,480
Hmm.

92
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:06,240
Anyway, like I was saying,

93
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:08,280
something's been bothering Kid lately.

94
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,800
He seems a bit suspicious of your recent actions.

95
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:15,360
He's been poking around for information on his own.

96
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:16,740
What should we do?

97
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:20,880
Poking around for information?

98
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,640
For information, that's right.

99
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,360
Hmm.

100
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,840
On his own?

101
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:30,200
Yes, on his own.

102
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:33,660
So, what should we do?

103
00:07:33,980 --> 00:07:35,080
That's what I asked.

104
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,260
It's a difficult question.

105
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,680
None of us like going into this blind.

106
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:40,520
Eh?

107
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:42,540
Kid's not the only one.

108
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,180
I want to know what's going on, too.

109
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,560
Why are you collecting all of Abon's tools?

110
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,560
Why haven't you explained yourself to us?

111
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:49,560
What's your plan?

112
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:52,000
You want to know my plan?

113
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,440
Yes, of course I do.

114
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:55,140
You want me to explain?

115
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:56,880
I want you to explain.

116
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,040
That's what I just said.

117
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:01,040
Too bad.

118
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,540
I'm not going to tell you.

119
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,020
How old are you, 11?

120
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,360
Sid, Lord Death.

121
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,060
Good morning.

122
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:10,900
Yo, Meister Maka.

123
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:12,140
Great to see you.

124
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,080
How's it hanging?

125
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,340
Um, Lord Death,

126
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:17,720
there's something I wanted to ask you about.

127
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,040
Is now a good time?

128
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:19,840
Of course.

129
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:20,680
Ask away.

130
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,960
What do you want to know?

131
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,600
I'll tell you anything.

132
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:25,880
Hey now, can I get some equality here?

133
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,020
A genie hunter technique?

134
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,000
Yes.

135
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:34,340
The old man mosquito seems surprised to see me using it.

136
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:36,040
I was trying to do witch hunter,

137
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:37,860
and then this other technique came out instead.

138
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:39,360
I don't understand.

139
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,260
Are the two related?

140
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:45,580
Oh, our little Meister Maka has learned how to use the genie hunter, has she?

141
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:46,440
Amazing.

142
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:48,820
Oh, it's not that big a deal.

143
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:50,600
They grow up so quickly.

144
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,680
You're becoming more like your mother every day.

145
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:54,420
Huh?

146
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:57,220
This new genie hunter technique of yours.

147
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:59,920
I've only ever seen one Meister do it before you,

148
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:01,580
and that was your mother, my dear.

149
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,320
Are you serious?

150
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:04,320
My mother?

151
00:09:04,660 --> 00:09:05,080
Yep.

152
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,340
As the name genie hunter suggests,

153
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:10,860
it's a special move that works against particularly evil forces.

154
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:14,860
Only a superior Meister like your mother could control it.

155
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:17,760
She truly was a talented young woman, you know.

156
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:20,920
Who would have thought you'd follow in her steps so quickly?

157
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:22,620
This is an amazing achievement.

158
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:23,520
Congratulations.

159
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:26,300
If you continue improving at this rate,

160
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:29,240
who knows, you may even be able to defeat the Kishen.

161
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,220
I don't know about that.

162
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:33,320
I know this game.

163
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,620
When I was alive, I too was very adept at flattery.

164
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,540
But this isn't over yet.

165
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:41,620
We still have a long way to go before victory is ours.

166
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:43,860
I expect you to keep working hard.

167
00:09:44,380 --> 00:09:44,820
Right.

168
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:46,620
See ya!

169
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:55,100
Following in my mother's footsteps.

170
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,620
Never thought Maka's abilities would awaken so soon.

171
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:01,620
This is incredible.

172
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:03,480
It's good news, indeed.

173
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,020
With a little more progress,

174
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:08,540
the power to annihilate the Kishen may very well be in her hands.

175
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,200
Anyway, Sid, back to business.

176
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,040
Sir?

177
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:14,140
The package we spoke of.

178
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,640
Has it been delivered yet?

179
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:17,180
What do you mean?

180
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,160
You remember?

181
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:18,880
The package.

182
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:23,240
I believe I asked you to locate a certain gentleman in Oceania and bring him here.

183
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,460
Oh, I get it now.

184
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,060
The package, of course.

185
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,940
It should be delivered very soon, sir.

186
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:28,840
Indeed.

187
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,040
That's good to hear.

188
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:33,560
Heedless of my own safety,

189
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,440
I plunged into the magnetic field.

190
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,720
And then there was a great explosion!

191
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,860
The terror of it would have made a lesser man weep.

192
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:41,920
Give me a break.

193
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,820
Like, that's really how it happened.

194
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:46,440
Sit down and shut your big, lying mouth!

195
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:47,880
Okay.

196
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:54,100
Was the battle on Lost Island really as difficult as Ox says it was?

197
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:54,760
Yes.

198
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:58,320
Skirmishes with arachnophobia broke out all over the island.

199
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,720
He should shut up.

200
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:02,260
I don't know what he thinks we have to be so proud of.

201
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:05,760
We failed, remember?

202
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:07,880
Arachnophobia has brew now.

203
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:10,240
We lost the fight that mattered.

204
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:15,320
Yeah, that's true, but it could have been worse.

205
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,160
Your piano playing was awesome, Sol.

206
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:19,500
Without that, who knows what would have happened to us.

207
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,040
Yep.

208
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:21,260
Look at it that way.

209
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,320
Everybody returned home safe and sound.

210
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,760
We managed to get away without anyone being hurt.

211
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:27,020
Surely that's more important.

212
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,400
Did we, though?

213
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:31,820
What about the professor?

214
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,600
I wonder how he's doing.

215
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,760
Do you mean Professor Stein?

216
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:37,580
Mm-hmm.

217
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,800
He collapsed suddenly while we were on the island.

218
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:42,200
It was frightening.

219
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:42,720
Oh.

220
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:45,480
He's probably at home recovering today.

221
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,340
I hope it's nothing serious.

222
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:50,040
What's happening to him?

223
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:51,720
Is it my fault?

224
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:56,200
If I hadn't planted that snake in Miss Marie's coffee,

225
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:58,520
would Professor Stein be okay still?

226
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,460
You look sick, Krona.

227
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,520
Is something wrong?

228
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:07,840
No, I'm fine.

229
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:10,580
It's nothing to worry about, really.

230
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,040
Nothing, nothing at all.

231
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:14,420
He's kind of an odd duck, isn't he?

232
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:16,800
Hey, Krona.

233
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,360
You should eat.

234
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:20,420
You're looking pale.

235
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,280
Uh, yeah.

236
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,340
What should I do?

237
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:38,300
Okay, what's going on?

238
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,740
Just come with me.

239
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:40,620
Why should I?

240
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:41,620
Where are we going?

241
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:42,860
Over there.

242
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,180
That's very specific.

243
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:44,740
Thanks.

244
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,100
Hurry up.

245
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:48,580
We need to practice it again before we forget how it works.

246
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:49,720
What are you talking about?

247
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:50,840
That new technique.

248
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,580
Lord Death thinks we might be able to use it to beat the Kishin.

249
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,120
Huh?

250
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,940
So we need extra practice.

251
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:56,480
Huh?

252
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,560
It's not there.

253
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:09,160
It's not there.

254
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:11,300
Don't you get it?

255
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,100
It's not there.

256
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:13,780
There.

257
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,160
That's better now.

258
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,900
Excuse me, Professor Stein.

259
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,100
Are you feeling okay?

260
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:19,880
Feeling okay?

261
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,480
Of course.

262
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:22,460
Why wouldn't I be?

263
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:28,940
Although I suppose saying that doesn't guarantee everyone will believe me, does it?

264
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,400
I want to ask you something.

265
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:36,600
What exactly does Brew do?

266
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:37,660
Can you tell me?

267
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:41,860
You already know that Brew is one of Ebon's magic tools.

268
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:48,240
He was a prominent inventor and created many impressive devices in his time, but Brew is the most powerful of them all.

269
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:53,160
True to its name, the tool's magic promises all the strength and danger of a brewing thunderstorm.

270
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:57,820
The results of its use can vary greatly depending on the person who wields it.

271
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,060
Be more specific.

272
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:01,940
I want to know what the tool actually does.

273
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:03,380
Is it there?

274
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:06,160
Tell me this, then.

275
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,260
What does my father plan to do with Brew?

276
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,480
What will the results be if he's the one who uses it?

277
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:13,700
If you aren't sure, you can speculate.

278
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,600
As a professor, you should have a guess.

279
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:22,480
What will you do with the information?

280
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:28,380
I can see that you're impatient for answers, but nothing I tell you will be of any use in the long run.

281
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:29,780
I can promise you that much.

282
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:34,100
Besides which, how could you fully accept whatever I might say while I'm in this condition?

283
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,360
Would that be a good idea?

284
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,420
Well, I don't know.

285
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:38,640
I'm sure you're willing to listen to my answers.

286
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:39,800
That's the easy part.

287
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,840
But then what comes after that?

288
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,940
What do you intend to do after you know all that I have to tell?

289
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,240
Extra practices aren't cool at all.

290
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:53,960
That kind of thing is only good for teachers, pets, and straight-A students.

291
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,900
Well, I am a straight-A student.

292
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,500
Now, would you transform into a scythe?

293
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,360
Come on, Sol!

294
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,680
All right, all right.

295
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:03,500
Quit whining.

296
00:15:03,700 --> 00:15:04,340
I'm doing it.

297
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:11,580
You ready?

298
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,500
Just waiting on you.

299
00:15:17,660 --> 00:15:19,440
Let's go, Sol Resonance!

300
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:29,320
Genie Hunter!

301
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:31,140
Huh?

302
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:33,220
That isn't right.

303
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,220
This is Witch Hunter.

304
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:36,520
Why isn't it becoming Genie Hunter?

305
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:49,160
Why didn't it work this time?

306
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:51,900
Are you being lazy because you don't feel like practicing?

307
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:53,280
Come off it, Maka.

308
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:55,740
If I was being lazy, how could we have done Witch Hunter?

309
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,500
Yeah, you have a point there.

310
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:58,780
But why then?

311
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:01,480
Maybe because we're not even sure how we did it the first time.

312
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:05,380
What's with the face?

313
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,340
A new technique always takes a little while.

314
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:09,940
Isn't that why we're practicing?

315
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:12,160
Yes.

316
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:16,560
Let's try it again.

317
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:17,820
Bring it on!

318
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:29,000
What is Arachne up to now?

319
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
She sent those little spiders of hers out everywhere.

320
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:33,620
They're all across the world.

321
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:36,040
She's up to something.

322
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:36,900
I'm sure of it.

323
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:39,220
Whatever her plan is, it's starting to move forward.

324
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:41,640
Thank you for reporting in.

325
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:45,540
If there's any further news, I'd appreciate being kept informed of the situation.

326
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:46,660
I'll let you know.

327
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,720
Things are moving along exactly as I'd hoped.

328
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:56,380
What else?

329
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,880
Have you noticed any changes?

330
00:16:58,220 --> 00:16:59,420
Uh, no.

331
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:01,400
I haven't seen anything out of the ordinary.

332
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,620
Well, have you at least found out the location of the secret vault?

333
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:05,940
Oh, yeah, that.

334
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:06,900
Not yet.

335
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:09,240
You should at least have something by now.

336
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,980
Do you want to stay with your pals at the Academy or not?

337
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,440
It's just...

338
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,020
Ribbit?

339
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:18,960
This whole business with the snake we planted inside Miss Marie.

340
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:19,880
The snake?

341
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:20,920
What about it?

342
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:22,960
Something's happening.

343
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:25,060
I think it's hurting Professor Stein.

344
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,020
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

345
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:28,720
It's working well.

346
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:30,460
You did a very good job with that.

347
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:34,300
We've got brew now, and it's all thanks to that little snake.

348
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:37,580
We've knocked one of the Academy's best Meisters out of the game,

349
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,760
and we didn't even have to get involved in the battle.

350
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,720
It's my fault.

351
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:43,340
I did this.

352
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:46,220
You're shivering.

353
00:17:46,340 --> 00:17:46,820
What's wrong?

354
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,560
No, I'm fine.

355
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:49,460
Good.

356
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,920
Now you should get going.

357
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,640
Don't you have more work to see to?

358
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:55,900
Medusa's counting on you, Crona.

359
00:17:57,100 --> 00:17:58,740
You wouldn't want to let her down.

360
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:11,220
That's enough.

361
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:13,700
I don't think we need to practice any more today.

362
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:20,080
Come on.

363
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:20,840
Let's go back.

364
00:18:21,580 --> 00:18:22,240
Get up.

365
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,720
I don't understand.

366
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:26,760
Why can't we do it?

367
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:27,680
Who knows?

368
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,560
We did it before.

369
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:30,440
Why not now?

370
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,300
We know it exists now.

371
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:33,160
That's what matters.

372
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,760
We did it once.

373
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,520
It's bound to happen again sooner or later.

374
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:41,220
Just not quite yet.

375
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,260
I'm so hungry I could eat a horse.

376
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,580
Which reminds me, it's your turn to cook dinner tonight.

377
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,280
I forgot to shop.

378
00:18:58,580 --> 00:18:59,300
We're out of food.

379
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:00,140
Why, you!

380
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,240
Sorry.

381
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:03,880
Looks like PB&J tonight.

382
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:05,520
You gotta be kidding me!

383
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:11,140
Right now, it doesn't matter what I want.

384
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:14,680
I can't ignore something just because I don't want to see it.

385
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:18,040
You can't turn a blind eye, not even for your own father?

386
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,620
I can't make exceptions.

387
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:22,380
Anyone who strays from the right path must be stopped.

388
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:25,960
But who decides which path is the right one?

389
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:29,160
And how do you recognize when someone has strayed from it?

390
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:29,900
It's simple.

391
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:32,620
The truth is easy to see when you know right from wrong.

392
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:34,240
Oh, is it really?

393
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,920
You're quite naive, aren't you?

394
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:38,920
About what?

395
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:40,520
Let me ask you this.

396
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,640
Where does this knowledge of yours come from?

397
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:44,480
This ability to know right and wrong?

398
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,680
There is no inherent good or evil in the world.

399
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:50,120
Those labels are just artificial constructs.

400
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:54,900
Right and wrong are determined by the people who hold positions of authority.

401
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:56,260
That's the way it's always been.

402
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:59,140
So how then can anyone know this truth you speak of?

403
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,420
Don't you see?

404
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:05,480
The reality is that truth long ago became nothing more than a shadow of itself.

405
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,360
It's a mere echo of the past now.

406
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:08,060
You're wrong.

407
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:09,280
Idealistic boy.

408
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:11,540
The world is one big moral gray area.

409
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:15,880
It just makes you feel safer to believe that it can be carefully categorized into good and bad.

410
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,500
That's not actually how it works.

411
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:18,400
You're wrong!

412
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:20,820
Why are you so determined about this, kid?

413
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:23,780
Why are you still refusing to answer any of my questions?

414
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:26,460
What information are you so desperate to keep hidden?

415
00:20:26,980 --> 00:20:27,240
Hmm.

416
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:33,460
Oh, hi, kid.

417
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:36,380
What's going on here?

418
00:20:38,160 --> 00:20:39,040
Say you're right.

419
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:43,180
Doesn't that still make the Academy the authority that determines what right and wrong are?

420
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:45,220
Huh.

421
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,760
Is that truly how you think it works?

422
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:56,120
On that point, I fear I must once again disagree with you completely.

423
00:20:57,140 --> 00:21:01,480
Things at the Academy aren't always as black and white as you'd like to believe they are.

424
00:21:09,040 --> 00:21:17,180
He's finally here.

425
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:19,540
Joe Butataki.

426
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:23,940
Technology consultant from the Oceaniaic Division of the DWMA.

427
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,620
Death City.

428
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:29,420
I made it.

429
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,780
My new workplace.

430
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,060
Well, let's get started.

431
00:21:35,060 --> 00:22:05,040
We'll be right back.

432
00:22:05,060 --> 00:22:35,040
We'll be right back.

433
00:22:35,060 --> 00:23:05,040
We'll be right back.

434
00:23:06,060 --> 00:23:08,920
Kid, you idiot. Have you found anything yet?

435
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:11,120
Soul sounds a little discontent.

436
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:13,320
Me? What are you talking about?

437
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,920
Discontent and angry.

438
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:15,800
Oh, please.

439
00:23:15,980 --> 00:23:17,840
Discontent, angry, and impatient.

440
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,360
Hey, I'm not... never mind.

441
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,960
And in denial, too.

442
00:23:22,840 --> 00:23:24,660
On the next episode of Soul Eater,

443
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,040
Ashura's temptation,

444
00:23:26,500 --> 00:23:28,180
the big man's uncontrollable irritation,

445
00:23:28,620 --> 00:23:30,540
Soul is desperate for attention.

446
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:32,840
Just stick to watch it or I'll take your soul.

447
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:34,100
That's my line.

